Package: apsimR
Title: APSIM Next Generation as a Contract-Emitting Analysis Member
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R:
    person("Max", "Moldovan", , "max.moldovan@adelaide.edu.au",
           role = c("aut", "cre", "cph"),
           comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0001-9680-8474"))
Description: A typed, server-capable R interface to APSIM Next Generation, the
    process-based agricultural systems simulator. Drives the simulator for
    prediction over scenario designs, mechanism-parameter estimation, parameter
    calibration against observations (a bounded optimiser, or an iterative
    ensemble smoother when 'PESTO' is present), global sensitivity analysis
    (Morris and Sobol), Gaussian-process emulation with leave-one-out
    diagnostics, validation against observations (goodness-of-fit metrics and a
    typed verdict), and the generation of known-causal-structure datasets for
    testing causal-inference methods, and returns results as a versioned,
    provenance-complete object
    compatible with the 'PESTO' ensemble-manifest contract, so simulator output
    composes directly with downstream calibration, uncertainty-quantification and
    causal-inference tools. Execution degrades gracefully: every entry point
    abstains with a typed reason when the simulator or its runtime is absent.
    The package's own sources are released under the MIT licence; when used with
    'apsimx' (GPL-3) or 'PESTO' (GPL (>= 3)) the installed combination is a
    combined work subject to the terms of the GPL (>= 3).
